title: Civil Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: cotus_affairs, cabinet
view-if: rep_majority = 1 and civil_rights_timer = 0
card-image: img/Freedmen.jpg
on-arrival: civil_rights_timer += 6;

= Radicals Demand a Civil Rights Act

[? civil_rights_act_passed = 0 : <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> are demanding that Congress pass sweeping civil rights legislation to protect freedmen from Southern "Black Codes" and ensure equality before the law. ?]

[? civil_rights_act_passed = 0 : They argue that Reconstruction means nothing without federal guarantees of citizenship, due process, and equal protection.?]

[? civil_rights_act_passed = 0 : <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> are divided. Some warn it will provoke a presidential veto and alienate <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> allies. Others say the time for compromise has passed. ?]

[? civil_rights_act_passed = 1 : With the passage of the Civil Rights acts, {!<span title="Unless your a women. Sorry Ladies">all citizens of the United States are to be treated equal under the law</span>!}. But revanchist southerners aim to ignore the law and continue there racist ways to preserve "White Man's Rule" in the South. ?]

[? civil_rights_act_passed = 1 : <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> are demanding that President exercise his executive powers to properly enforce the law across the south. ?]

What will we do???

- @pass_civil_rights: Back the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical**</span> push and pass the Act.
- @enforce: Enforce the Civil Rights Acts
- @stall_civil_rights: Delay action for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@pass_civil_rights
subtitle: -2 budget & Congress majority
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 2: Not enough budget. ?][? if house_majority < 2: We don't have a House majority. ?][? if sen_majority < 2: We don't have a Senate majority. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and house_majority > 1 and sen_majority > 1
view-if: civil_rights_act_passed = 0
on-arrival: civil_rights_act_passed = 1; budget -= 2; PoliticalCostPenalty += 2; veto += 1; veto_reason = "Civil Rights Act"; freedmen_rep += 5; radical_strength += 5; moderate_dissent += 3; conservative_dissent += 4; liberal_dissent += 3; civil_rights += 5;

We endorse the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals'**</span> initiative and pass the Civil Rights Act through Congress. It marks a bold stand for equality—but may force a veto showdown with the President.

@enforce
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 2: Not enough budget. ?][? if president_party != "rep": We don't control the executive. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 1 and president_party = "rep"
view-if: civil_rights_act_passed = 1
on-arrival: civil_rights += 3; kkk_strength -= 3; whiteL_strength -= 1.5; radical_strength += 3;

We continue to enforce the civil rights act across the country to ensure the freedmen are treated equal.

@stall_civil_rights
subtitle: <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderate**</span> Stability
on-arrival: radical_dissent += 5; moderate_strength += 3; freedmen_rep -= 3;

We decide not to move forward—yet. <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> appreciate our restraint, but <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> allies and Black communities grow increasingly impatient.



